      "text": "Bogotá: red, white and yellow buses on a busy street"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:ca0a4d6daf445776",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ed1149e1c5d3de062f9fedce7aa433c6e56bb52d71892015b075f93a6d1ff118",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw9nvgw6-cx25ndvy",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Hacienda Coloma and Coffee Tour"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2309e54c4c130f6ab91e14718c821291850b6ed7e220fe42e357fb97cea302aa",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw9nvgw6-cx25ndvy",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, meet your English-speaking guide in the hotel lobby. You’ll head to Hacienda Coloma near Fusagasugá. The drive from Bogotá takes around 120 minutes.\n\nThe day focuses on coffee production. During the tour, you’ll see the main stages, from seeds and growing coffee plants to harvesting the beans and brewing coffee. You’ll see a working coffee farm and learn what gives Colombian coffee its flavour.\n\nAfter the coffee tour, the programme continues in the cellar, where you’ll taste an eight-year-old rum with notes of coffee.\n\nA traditional regional lunch is included at the end of the tour. Afterwards, return to Bogotá and spend the rest of the day at leisure."
    }
  ]
